    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the prime factorisation of $540$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$540=2^2\\times3^3\\times5$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}540&=2\\times270\\\\540&=2^2\\times135\\\\540&=2^2\\times3\\times45\\\\540&=2^2\\times3^2\\times15\\\\540&=2^2\\times3^3\\times5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, show that $540$ has twenty-four factors.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(2+1)(3+1)(1+1)=24$ factors.",
          "worked": "Every factor of $540=2^2\\times3^3\\times5$ has the form $2^a3^b5^c$, where $a=0,1,2$, $b=0,1,2,3$ and $c=0,1$. There are three choices for $a$, four for $b$ and two for $c$.\n\nThe number of factors is $3\\times4\\times2=24$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the least natural number with twenty-four factors.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$360=2^3\\times3^2\\times5$.\n\nIts prime exponents give $4\\times3\\times2=24$ factors; comparing the possible exponent patterns establishes the minimum.",
          "worked": "For $N=p_1^{e_1}\\cdots p_k^{e_k}$, the number of factors is $(e_1+1)\\cdots(e_k+1)$. To minimise $N$, use the smallest primes and place the largest exponent on the smallest prime.\n\nThe possible exponent patterns and their least numbers are:\n\n$(23)$: $2^{23}=8388608$;\n\n$(11,1)$: $2^{11}\\times3=6144$;\n\n$(7,2)$: $2^7\\times3^2=1152$;\n\n$(5,3)$: $2^5\\times3^3=864$;\n\n$(5,1,1)$: $2^5\\times3\\times5=480$;\n\n$(3,2,1)$: $2^3\\times3^2\\times5=360$;\n\n$(2,1,1,1)$: $2^2\\times3\\times5\\times7=420$.\n\nEach pattern gives twenty-four factors. The least number is therefore $360$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 92
      }
    ]
  },
